  "author": "whirligig",
  "version": "1",
  "notes": "A 2 kg autogyro: free-spinning teetering rotor on a mast raked 9 degrees back, a pusher propeller, and a small electric pre-rotator that spins the head up before the takeoff roll and then drops out - the rotor is UNPOWERED in flight, kept turning entirely by the airflow (PLAN Phase 4). Control is cyclic on the free head plus a rudder on the fin, like the full-size machines. Nothing in the engine knows what an autogyro is; the mast rake and the free shaft are the whole trick.",
